            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "Today (Friday, **July 31, 2026**) the biggest “Azure AI” news is tied to Microsoft’s just-reported results and a few very recent Azure AI platform announcements:\n\n## 1) Azure growth is being driven by AI demand (earnings/news today)\nMultiple reports today point to **accelerating Azure growth attributed to enterprise AI adoption**, following Microsoft’s latest quarterly results—driving a notable move in Microsoft’s stock. ([msn.com](https://www.msn.com/en-us/money/other/azure-ignites-microsoft-stock-ai-fueled-earnings-beat-sparks-9-rally/ar-AA294cLq))\n\n## 2) Official Azure AI infrastructure expansion with AMD (announced July 20, 2026)\nMicrosoft published an official post about **expanding Azure AI and HPC infrastructure with AMD**, positioning it as part of scaling capacity for model and agentic workloads. ([blogs.microsoft.com](https://blogs.microsoft.com/blog/2026/07/20/microsoft-expands-azure-ai-and-hpc-infrastructure-with-amd/))\n\n## 3) Microsoft + Mistral partnership expansion (announced July 21, 2026)\nMicrosoft also announced an expanded strategic partnership with **Mistral**, aimed at giving enterprises (including regulated industries) “frontier AI they can control,” which is directly relevant to Azure-hosted AI options. ([news.microsoft.com](https://news.microsoft.com/source/2026/07/21/microsoft-and-mistral-expand-strategic-partnership-to-give-enterprises-and-regulated-industries-frontier-ai-they-can-control/))\n\n## 4) What Microsoft lists as the freshest “Azure AI” product updates\nIf you want the most literal “latest updates,” Microsoft’s **Azure Updates** feed is the canonical rolling changelog across Azure services (including AI/ML). ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/updates/))\n\n---\n\nIf you tell me what you mean by “Azure AI” (e.g., **Azure AI Foundry**, **Azure OpenAI Service**, **Azure AI Search**, **Document Intelligence**, **Content Safety**, etc.), I can filter to just that product area and summarize only the last 24–72 hours.",
